    5 | "trolling grain starts, windows, overlap, jitter, per-grain HF smoothing, and post-grain cleanup.\n// v37 PerfGate: Grain corpus build is lazy/gated to Granular mode, dead learned-flow training is disabled, and Granular runtime selection plus 32-slot grain scans are gated so Raw/Tape/Hybrid avoid corpus work and Hybrid avoids Granular slot cost.\n// v36 GranStretch EventScale + PeakPack Pro: in Granular only, Stretch is repurposed from fast purposeful grains at 1x toward slower, larger, more coherent event playback at 4x; Raw/Tape/Hybrid Stretch behavior is preserved.\n// v35 MacroGrain OLAGlue + PeakPack Pro: Granular adds 1ms/10ms/100ms/1000ms-scale load-time corpus analysis, permits event-scale macro-grains for coherent SFX, and smooths OLA/spawn edges to reduce clicks and gaps.\n// v49 PostEQSoloFix: restores Ctrl+click/drag temporary Post-EQ band/cut solo audition.\n// v28 SpectrumPrePost: Post-Processing now draws detailed pre-EQ and post-EQ spectra on one shared scale.\n// v50 AttackReleaseMinimal: note-off during Attack uses the user Release time, without retrigger interruption or changing release grain behavior.\n// v27 SpectrumDetail: Post-EQ spectrum uses a 96-bin resonant analyzer and thin trace drawing instead of a broad lowpass-difference blob.\n// v26 SpectrumContrast: Post-EQ spectrum underlay is brighter, adaptive, and easier to read on quiet material.\n// v61 PostEQ Character Fix: per-filter Character/Drive are front-buffered as independent values; Drive no longer pops between selected bands.\n// v60 PostEQ Ladder Character: Post-EQ bands can add Clean/Transistor/Diode driven band character with per-band drive.\n// v62 ColorERBTilt: the old Color macro is replaced by a zero-bypass ERB Tilt EQ. Tilt uses slider6; Alt+Color sets Pivot; Shift+Color toggles auto-infer pivot.\n// v25 BandQCal: Band 1/2/3 Q is calibrated to the actual peaking-biquad response; default Q is tighter and less absurdly wide.\n// v24 PostEQ QFix: HPF/LPF Q now produces visible and audible cutoff resonance, including 6 dB/oct mode.\n// v23 FreeBand PostEQ: three free parametric bands plus HPF/LPF, graph control, Q/slope gestures, and spectrum underlay.\n// v22 PostEQ removed the Shaper page and kept Processing as final-output EQ.\n// v19 AutoRelease: sample-tail analysis adds a release floor and graceful EOF/tail-grain fades.\n// v18 FormantDrive: Shift+drag Pitch controls an audible hidden transient-safe formant/resonance shift.\n// v13 CrossFlow: keeps v12 learned continuation, but prevents same-take reconstruction loops.\n// Slot 0 is the load-and-go sample bank.\n// Use the filename slot UI for this instrument and choose Open Multiple... on slot 0.\n// #FILE: Sample Bank {Open Multiple... loads the whole bank into slot 0; the bank auto-rescans when the selection changes.}\nfilename:0,sample.wav\n\n// #HELP: # Sample\n// #HELP:\n// #HELP: ## What it is\n// #HELP: Sample is a load-and-go psycho multisampler: load files into slot 0, play notes, and shape the bank with compact macro controls.\n// #HELP: v15 BrightCal uses a filterbank brightness meter and bank-aware Color scaling.\n// #HELP: v16 FocusCal makes Focus bank-aware: high attack-focus banks soften harder and clarify more cautiously; dull banks clarify harder and soften more cautiously.\n// #HELP: v18 strengthens Shift+drag Pitch formant shifting: audible spectral-envelope warp plus resonance drive, still transient-protected. Alt+drag Pitch controls Pitch Mix, a latency-aligned unpitched/pitched parallel blend.\n// #HELP: v19 AutoRelease analyzes each sample tail, extends too-short MIDI releases when needed, and fades source endings so EOF does not chop.\n// #HELP: v28 SpectrumPrePost shows both pre-EQ and post-EQ spectra with a cleaner high-resolution analyzer.\n// #HELP: v27 SpectrumDetail makes the Post-Processing spectrum sharper with a higher-resolution resonant analyzer and thinner trace display.\n// #HELP: v26 SpectrumContrast makes the Post-Processing spectrum underlay br"
