    6 | "ighter and easier to read on quiet material.\n// #HELP: v29 GrainCorpus builds a load-time grain/event corpus so Granular can transform both single long sources and multi-source banks without doing descriptor analysis at playback time.\n// #HELP: v33 EnvTrajectory teaches Granular to follow learned corpus energy motion so phrases have rises, falls, crests, and decay instead of flat wet grain beds.\n// #HELP: v46 CleanDeCrust adds Shift+drag Clean as an FFT-512 spectral-kurtosis decrust mode for crunchy/crusty SFX. It is intentionally fail-fast at high values and the FFT path is inactive unless the hidden mode is nonzero.\n// #HELP: v40 CleanScrub makes Clean a stronger general cleanup control: it detects low-SNR/sustained bed noise per band, suppresses hiss and static tails harder, preserves attacks, and becomes deliberately obvious at high values.\n// #HELP: v39 RoomScrub makes Room Tame a stronger general de-room control: it detects late/diffuse band energy, trims low-mid/presence room wash, narrows roomy side smear, and protects attacks.\n// #HELP: v51 SpaceVerb adds Shift+drag Room as hidden Space amount and Alt+drag Room as hidden Space character: scrub bad room with Room, then add intentional sound-design space.\n// #HELP: v57 SpaceVerb SoftRollback returns SpaceVerb to the subtler v54-style voice-send balance; Shift+Room/Alt+Room state still persists through render/sample-rate rebuilds via v56 hidden sliders.\n// #HELP: v66 Auto Smooth A/R adds an Envelope button that uses a fixed 25 ms causal transition budget. When enabled, Attack and Release become the ratio of that transition for smoother same-note crossfades and note-offs without MIDI lookahead/PDC.\n// #HELP: v52 Harmonics adds Shift+drag Output as a clean 8-band psychoacoustic harmonic enrichment macro: it generates a parallel, band-limited harmonic layer instead of driving the dry signal into saturation, and it is bypassed at 0.\n// #HELP: v38 DenormalGuard protects internal recursive filters/analyzers from near-zero denormal stalls, gates silent spectrum analysis, and preserves v37 Granular gating.\n// #HELP: v58 EdgeMelt replaces the old Shift+Grain input-trigger mode with a Granular-only grain-edge smoothing macro: safer starts, smoother windows, more overlap, less jitter, and post-grain micro-edge cleanup.\n// #HELP: v34 MultiScaleEventGrains analyzes short/mid/long windows at corpus-build time and lets Granular use event-sized grains when the source material wants continuity.\n// #HELP: v35 MacroGrain OLAGlue extends this to micro/short/mid/long/ultra windows, allowing coherent slow material to use 100 ms to 1 s grains while smoothing OLA starts, normalization, and long-grain window shape.\n// #HELP: v37 PerfGate lazily builds the GrainCorpus only when Granular mode is active or selected, disables obsolete learned-flow training, and caps Hybrid grain scans below the Granular-only 32-slot pool.\n// #HELP: v36 GranStretch repurposes Stretch inside Granular only: 1x keeps the current fast purposeful grain feel, while higher values bias toward slower, larger, more coherent event playback.\n// #HELP: v25 BandQCal makes Band 1/2/3 Q use the actual peaking-EQ response and changes the default from ultra-wide to generous.\n// #HELP: v24 PostEQ QFix makes HPF/LPF Q visible and audible as cutoff resonance.\n// #HELP: v23 FreeBand PostEQ adds a spectrum-underlaid final EQ: HPF, LPF, and three draggable parametric bands with Q and cutoff slope control.\n// #HELP:\n// #HELP: ## Quick start\n// #HELP: 1. Insert Sample. 2. On slot 0, choose Open Multiple... and select files. 3. Play MIDI notes. 4. Choose Random, Sequence, or Walk. 5. Shape with Envelope, Playback, Post-Processing, Clean, Room Tame, Anti-Salience, and Output.\n// #HELP:\n// #HELP: ## Selection modes\n// #HELP: Random picks from the full bank with anti-repeat weighting. Sequence steps through loaded files. Walk bridges from the previous sample using brightness, focus, transient richness, length, pitch confid"
