    7 | "ence, body span, and tail span.\n// #HELP:\n// #HELP: ## Envelope\n// #HELP: Attack, Hold, Decay, Sustain, and Release shape each trigger. Shift+Wheel on Attack, Decay, or Release changes slope from -100% to +100%; 0% is linear. Release is also protected by sample-dependent AutoRelease when a source would otherwise chop; Shift+drag Release changes hidden Tail Grace. The Auto Smooth A/R button converts Attack/Release into a 25 ms transition ratio for smoother back-to-back retriggers.\n// #HELP:\n// #HELP: ## Playback engines\n// #HELP: Raw plays the source directly. Tape uses the slower/heavier rate path. Hybrid keeps the head direct, sustains from body grains, can borrow matched tails, and can hand off Release level/body phase into the next Attack. Granular uses a load-time analyzed grain corpus: long files become many searchable micro-events, multi-source banks become one shared grain field, and playback uses anchor/texture/spice streams, phrase + envelope trajectories, corpus continuity, source-adaptive overlap, restrained swells, release blooms, and grain-level decorrelation.\n// #HELP:\n// #HELP: Sample reports a constant latency of 520 engine samples (10.83 ms at 48 kHz, 1x); dry input and the final DeCrust stage are aligned.\n// #HELP:\n// #HELP: ## Cleanup and depth\n// #HELP: Clean is a transient-protected de-noise/de-bed macro: low values clean hiss/static tails gently, high values aggressively scrub low-SNR sustained noise and become obvious quickly. Shift+drag Clean controls DeCrust, a hidden FFT-512 spectral-kurtosis crust repair mode for crunchy SFX; at 0 it is fully bypassed with zero added latency. Enabling it selects 520-engine-sample latency; live toggles briefly fade while the host updates PDC. Room Tame is a transient-protected de-room/de-smear macro: low values restrain late room wash, high values make the correction obvious quickly. Shift+drag Room adds intentional designed Space; Alt+drag Room changes Space character from tight early room to wide dark bloom. Anti-Salience sets overall Mix. Ctrl+click selects Legacy or one of 20 Anti-Salience MX source/style combinations; right-click sets Mix to 0 and Ctrl+right-click selects Legacy. Shift/Alt expose no other mode.\n// #HELP:\n// #HELP: Legacy EQ import: Shift+right-click Drive imports the retained v60 preset value; Alt+right-click imports v61-v67. The two old formats overlap, so select the version that saved your preset. Values already rounded by an older host cannot be recovered exactly.\n// #HELP:\n// #HELP: ## Post-Processing\n// #HELP: The Post-Processing panel is a final-output EQ editor with pre/post spectrum overlay, draggable HPF/LPF cutoffs, and three free parametric bands. Drag bands horizontally for frequency and vertically for gain; wheel adjusts Q; Shift+Wheel on HPF/LPF changes slope; Ctrl+click/drag temporarily solos the selected band/cut for auditioning.\n// #HELP:\n// #HELP: ## Tone and feel\n// #HELP: Color is now ERB Tilt: positive brightens, negative darkens around a pivot. Alt+Color sets Pivot; Shift+Color toggles auto-infer pivot. Focus softens/clarifies. Shift+drag Focus adjusts hidden Peak Pack: negative can flatten detected spectral maxima, positive can push resonant maxima. Shift+drag Pitch adjusts hidden formant/resonance shift. Shift+drag Grain adjusts hidden Edge Melt for Granular-only grain-border smoothing. Width spreads safely. Liveliness adds variation; Shift+drag/wheel sets Thrill, a separate 0-15% Accent Engine injection defaulting to 0. Truth moves from matched behavior toward raw sample individuality. Dynamics adds density with protection; Shift+drag/wheel Dynamics sets Universal Contour aggression for joint tail, resonance and eligible breath cleanup, with full bypass at 0. Shift+drag Output adds clean parallel Harmonics.\n// #HELP:\n// #HELP:\n// #HELP: ## Best uses\n// #HELP: Fast one-shot banks, found-sound instruments, texture instruments, sketching, and exploratory sound design.\n// #HELP:\n// #HELP: ## Wrong too"
